  "description": "Debug a deployed ASP.NET Core application on your own machine, without redeploying. Add two lines\n      to the app and incoming HTTP requests are handed to a locally running copy, so you can set\n      breakpoints on real traffic from a real caller; disconnect and the deployed app serves requests\n      itself again.\n\n      This is the half that goes into your application. It pairs with the WormholeRelay desktop client,\n      a portable Windows exe from the GitHub releases page - neither half does anything alone.\n\n      For debugging only, and only on systems you are authorised to debug. Off unless the host\n      explicitly enables it for a named environment with a joining key, and never to be enabled in\n      production. See the readme before using it on any shared environment.",
